<LegalPage title="Terms of Service - Doer" description="Terms for the Doer website and software." heading="Doer Terms of Service" lede="These terms describe the Doer website and software and the responsibilities that come with running tasks on your computer." effectiveDate="2026-10-07" lastUpdated="2026-10-07" sections={sections}>
  <section id="operator"><h2>Operator and scope</h2><p>Doer and <a href="https://doer.lagaryan.click">doer.lagaryan.click</a> are operated by Aryan Gupta and Aditya Mayank Sinha in India, reachable at <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>. The Microsoft Store publisher display name is Baandra. Doer is independent of T3 Tools, Inc., Microsoft and the AI providers it can connect to.</p></section>
  <section id="use"><h2>Using Doer</h2><p>Use Doer only with accounts, devices and files you own or have permission to access. Do not use it to send spam, impersonate others, violate privacy, distribute malware or break applicable laws or third-party terms. You are responsible for instructions you give, devices you pair and actions you approve. Doer is not directed to children under 13.</p></section>
  <section id="providers"><h2>AI providers and tools</h2><p>You choose and arrange access to third-party AI providers. Their availability, pricing, usage limits and terms apply separately. Doer is free to download; provider subscriptions, usage and your own hosting may incur charges. Prompts, file contents, context and tool results needed for tasks may be sent to the provider you select. Optional WSL use requires Windows Subsystem for Linux and a compatible configured distribution.</p><p>AI outputs can be wrong. Review document changes, recipients and other consequential actions before approving them. Keep backups of important files and do not edit the same file simultaneously in another app.</p></section>
  <section id="license"><h2>Open-source license</h2><p>Doer's software is distributed under the <a href="https://github.com/LAG-4/doer/blob/lite/LICENSE">MIT License</a>. Its license and upstream copyright notices remain applicable to copies and modifications. These website terms do not reduce your rights under that license. You retain rights in your content and files.</p></section>
  <section id="responsibility"><h2>Availability and responsibility</h2><p>The software is provided “as is” and “as available,” subject to the MIT License and rights applicable law does not allow to be excluded. Features may change, services may be interrupted and third-party access may expire or be revoked. The operator does not promise that AI outputs are correct or every task or document format is supported.</p><p>You can stop using Doer at any time. Disconnect connected services and remove local application data separately if you wish to end access and delete stored information. See our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for data handling, analytics and deletion choices.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>Updates will be published here with a revised date. Questions and support: Aryan Gupta, <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>; Aditya Mayank Sinha, <a href="mailto:adityamayank708@gmail.com">adityamayank708@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
